            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Tamil for let's go, then the Tamil for a holiday."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: விடைபெறுகிறேன்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "விடைபெறுகிறேன் (viṭaipeṟukiṟēṉ) — \"I take my leave\", literally \"I receive leave\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "விடை is \"leave, permission\". The formal goodbye."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "விடைபெறுகிறேன் (viṭaipeṟukiṟēṉ) is native: viṭai, \"leave, permission to go\" (DEDR 5393), and peṟu, \"to get\" (DEDR 4422): \"I get my leave\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A formal way out of a room."
            }
          ]
        },
